%% coins_boot.glp --- the currency on two smartphones (SGSG paper, Section 7):
%% under the boot harness, one isolate per person, each with its own key pair,
%% running the social graph of graph/core as its super-app and hosting
%% Currencies' mini-app (programs/coins/currency).  Each person trusts the
%% bundled compiler's key, reads the certified artefact currency.glpw from
%% graph/core with load_file/2 and installs it, giving the super-app one end of
%% a channel of the mediator's cards and the person's answers; alice cold-calls
%% bob, they befriend across the isolates, alice invites bob to the currency,
%% bob consents, and the handshake opens a root channel of the currency's own
%% protocol between their two executions, each activated by run/3.  Each person
%% then mints 2 and alice swaps her 2 for bob's 2, bob accepting --- the
%% currency's own swap, over the conversation the social graph delivered
%% between two smartphones.  The program is graph/core, named as :boot's second
%% argument:
%%   :artefact programs/coins/currency programs/social/graph/core
%%   :boot programs/social/coins_boot.glp programs/social/graph/core
%% Expected on the persons' screens: [alice] opened(bob), [alice] minted(2),
%% [bob] opened(alice), [bob] minted(2), [alice] swap_done(bob),
%% [bob] swap_done(alice), and the holdings each side of the swap.

procedure boot.
boot :-
    sg_init(alice, coins, _)@alice,
    sg_init(bob, coins, _)@bob.
